; step_limit_zero: a budget of exactly zero executes nothing.
;
; The limit is exact, so zero is a real budget and not a sentinel for
; "unbounded". No vector anywhere else uses 0, and a falsy-guard form
; that reads it as unlimited leaves every other vector green.
;
; The first instruction is refused, so the run faults before the ADD
; that would otherwise leave 3 on the stack.

PUSH 1
PUSH 2
ADD
